For the macOS builds only: apply to DPF before building (see BUILDING-MACOS.md and .github/workflows/macos.yml).

    patch -p1 -d dpf < patches/dpf-macos-focus.patch

Made against DPF 4238e1c. What it changes in a plugin's window on macOS:

- A key the plugin has no use for goes on to the host. Without this the plugin's view keeps every key once it
  has been clicked in, so that space no longer starts the host and its shortcuts stop working until something
  outside the plugin is clicked. A key the UI does take (typing a preset name) stays with the plugin.
- A click in a plugin window that is not the active one works at once, instead of only making the window active.

